# Keys this base needs. Copy to .env and fill in; never commit the filled-in .env.
#
# Graded-runtime key (the agent under evaluation). Set the one your Worker runs on:
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY  if the floor is on the Claude Agent SDK (the lab's default Path A).
#   OPENAI_API_KEY     if the floor is on the OpenAI Agents SDK (Path B), AND it is the
#                      grader/judge backend for DeepEval, Ragas, and the OpenAI Evals API.
#   The judge and the graded model must differ (no self-grading); set both keys if your
#   graded runtime is Claude but your judge is OpenAI (a common, recommended split).
#   OpenAI-compatible providers (DeepSeek, OpenRouter) for the cheap pre-record harness
#   also set OPENAI_BASE_URL.
#
# Phoenix collector (Decision 7). Local Phoenix needs NEITHER of these; it is keyless on
#   localhost. Set them only if you point traces at Phoenix Cloud instead of local.
#   PHOENIX_COLLECTOR_ENDPOINT  e.g. http://localhost:6006/v1/traces (default if unset).
#   PHOENIX_API_KEY             Phoenix Cloud only; omit for local.
#
# DATABASE_URL    the pgvector store for TutorClaw (Decision 5). You do not fill this by
#   hand: the agent provisions your Neon over the Neon MCP, then writes DATABASE_URL here.
#
# CONFIDENT_API_KEY  OPTIONAL, OFF BY DEFAULT. Only if you opt into the hosted Confident AI
#   DeepEval MCP (beta). Not required for any Decision; the local DeepEval pytest path needs
#   no Confident AI account. Leave blank unless you deliberately wire the hosted MCP.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
PHOENIX_COLLECTOR_ENDPOINT=
PHOENIX_API_KEY=
CONFIDENT_API_KEY=
